==Icelandic==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[afhverju]] (''wrong'')

===Etymology===
From ''[[af]]'' (meaning "[[of]]") + ''[[hverju]]'' (meaning "[to] [[what]]"), the {{dat}} {{singular}} neuter of ''[[hver]]'' (meaning "[[who]]"). Literally meaning "[[of]] [[what]]".

===Adverb===
'''[[af]] [[hver]]ju'''

# [[why]]?
#* ''[[mamma|Mamma]], '''af hverju''' [[vera|er]] [[himinn|himininn]] [[blár]]?''
#*: [[mommy|Mommy]], '''why''' [[be|is]] the [[sky]] [[blue]]?
#* '''''Af hverju''' [[muna|myndirðu]] [[vilja]] [[fara]] [[til]] [[Spánn|Spánar]]?'' - [[af hverju ekki|Af hverju ekki]]?
#*: '''Why''' [[would]] [you] [[want]] to [[go]] [[to]] [[Spain]]? - [[why not|Why not]]?
#* '''''Af hverju''' [[mæta#Icelandic|mætirðu]] [[ekki#Icelandic|ekki]] [[í#Icelandic|í]] [[veisla|veisluna]]?''
#*: '''Why won't''' you [[go]] to the [[party]]?

====Synonyms====
*[[hvers vegna]]
*[[hví]]
*[[því]] (''colloquial'')

